# ASYSMA Self-Contained Production Record

## 1 — Composition

XMC composes a self-contained `.asysma` artifact containing the common ASYSMA layout, manifest, application identity, icon, target-native bootstrap, compiled payload, and integrity information.

## 2 — Native execution

The embedded bootstrap validates the artifact and delegates execution of the internal native program to the operating system's native loader facilities. The bootstrap does not replace the OS loader.

## 3 — Cross-platform execution

The build selects the appropriate native boundary for Linux/ELF, Windows/PE, or macOS/Mach-O. The common manifest identifies target and payload layout while native bootstrap implementation remains platform-specific.

## 4 — Independent application

A correctly composed artifact is intended to launch without SecureJDK28, XMC, or a website download being required. An installed XMC/ASYSMA runtime remains a supported spring, association, diagnostics, and integration path.

## Verification

Source contracts have been added. Native standalone execution is a local-build verification gate and must be tested on each supported target before being represented as production-complete.